  "question_stem": "A particle of mass $0.6\\text{ kg}$ is placed on a rough plane which is inclined at an angle of $21^{\\circ}$ to the horizontal. The particle is kept in equilibrium by a force of magnitude $P\\text{ N}$ acting parallel to a line of greatest slope of the plane, as shown in the diagram. The coefficient of friction between the particle and the plane is $0.3$. Show that the least possible value of $P$ is $0.470$, correct to 3 significant figures, and find the greatest possible value of $P$.",
